{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.CyclotomicStrandDoubling","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.CyclotomicStrandDoubling","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Polynomial.Cyclotomic.Eval"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_irreducible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_irreducible","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L163-L170","doc":"Φ_8 is irreducible over ℚ.  Standard cyclotomic-irreducibility\nfact; relevant because the (D − n) Habiro element contains\nΦ_8² as a factor — the square indicates a multiplicity-2\nstructural appearance, not a polynomial-degree property. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.isospin_signature_distinct_from_deuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.isospin_signature_distinct_from_deuteron","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L140-L161","doc":"The cross-pair finding: the (n − p) signature `(X² − 1)` factor is\ndistinct from the deuteron-step signature `Φ_8²`.  This is the\nstructural distinction between isospin SU(2)_I and atomic-number\njumps observed in the (D − n) / (D − p) cross-pair audit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.isospin_classical_limit_kill","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.isospin_classical_limit_kill","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L126-L138","doc":"The isospin \"classical-limit kill\" factor:\n`Φ_1 · Φ_2 = (X - 1)(X + 1) = X² - 1`.\n\nThis is the cyclotomic prefactor identified in the (n − p)\nHabiro element factorization\n(`docs/audits/2026-05-31-qbeta-habiro-delta-am-factorization.md`).\nThe factor vanishes at X = 1 (classical limit q = 1), encoding\nthe fact that proton and neutron coincide classically: it is the\nbar-involution-paired isospin doublet structure made manifest. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_2","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L121-L124","doc":"The 2nd cyclotomic polynomial: `Φ_2(X) = X + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_1","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L116-L119","doc":"The 1st cyclotomic polynomial: `Φ_1(X) = X - 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_pow_two_strand_doubling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_pow_two_strand_doubling","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L86-L114","doc":"General strand-doubling identity for powers-of-two cyclotomic\npolynomials:  `Φ_{2^{k+1}}(X) = Φ_{2^k}(X²)` for `k ≥ 1`.\n\nThis is the structural pattern hypothesised in\n`docs/audits/2026-06-01-qbeta-habiro-phi8-interpretation.md`\nfor the cyclotomic prefactor of A=k → A=k+1 atomic-step pairs\nin the canonical Q_β Habiro element framework. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_eq_cyclotomic_4_comp_X_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8_eq_cyclotomic_4_comp_X_sq","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L70-L84","doc":"Strand-doubling cyclotomic identity over ℤ:\n`Φ_8(X) = Φ_4(X²)`.\n\nThis is the load-bearing algebraic identity for the categorical\ninterpretation of `Φ_8² = (X^4+1)²` in the deuteron's (D − n)\nHabiro element factorization.  The substitution `X → X²` is the\nstrand-doubling map lifting B_2 (2-strand single nucleon) to\nB_4 (4-strand deuteron, 2 nucleons × 2 isospin channels). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:cyclotomic-strand-doubling","label":"prop:cyclotomic-strand-doubling","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_8","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L58-L68","doc":"The 8th cyclotomic polynomial: `Φ_8(X) = X^4 + 1`.  Squared\nfactor identified in the (D − n) Habiro element factorization\n(`docs/audits/2026-05-31-qbeta-habiro-cross-pair-quick-dp.md`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CyclotomicStrandDoubling.cyclotomic_4","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/cyclotomic-strand-doubling.lean#L46-L56","doc":"The 4th cyclotomic polynomial: `Φ_4(X) = X² + 1`.  Single-nucleon\ndenominator factor identified in\n`habiro-coefficients-atomic.witness.json` for proton and neutron. ","signatureChunk":0}]}